        "original_id": "af50c12f-0a6d-5359-89e2-c44a53f175b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bear Lane, Christ Church, Oxford, Bear Inn, Oxford, Alfred Street, Blue Boar Street, Oxford, England\n- Organizations: University of Oxford\n- Concepts: Latin names\n\nFacts:\n- Christ Church, Oxford, is a constituent college of the University of Oxford in England.\n- Christ Church, Oxford, has the Latin name \"Ædes Christi,\" meaning the temple or house of Christ, and it is sometimes known as \"The House.\"\n- Bear Lane is located just north of Christ Church in Oxford.\n- The circa-17th-century incarnation of Bear Inn, Oxford, stands on the corner of Alfred Street and Blue Boar Street in central Oxford.\n- Bear Inn, Oxford, stands opposite Bear Lane and just north of Christ Church.",
